# Lumen Project Rules

Read @architecture.md before starting any task. It contains the full system design, API contract, and feature specs.

## Identity

Lumen is a network data ingestor/analyzer. React + TypeScript frontend against an existing FastAPI backend. Air-gapped LAN deployment — no external CDN calls in production code.

## Hard Rules

- TypeScript strict mode. No `any` types without `// JUSTIFY: <reason>` on the same line.
- API calls ONLY through `services/` layer. Components never call `fetch()` directly.
- All interactive UI primitives use Radix UI (`@radix-ui/react-*`).
- No external CDN imports in production code. Every dependency must be bundleable by Vite.
- File upload orchestration lives in `components/FileUpload.tsx`. Upload state machine in `hooks/useFileUpload.ts`. Do not scatter upload logic elsewhere.
- Server-side pagination for any dataset over 10k rows. Never load unbounded data client-side.
- URLs come from env vars `VITE_BASE_URL` and `VITE_WS_URL`. Never hardcode URLs.

## Architecture

```
services/   → ALL fetch/WS calls (api.ts, datasets.ts, query.ts, ws.ts)
hooks/      → state machines and subscriptions (useFileUpload, useWebSocket, useQueryHistory)
components/ → UI only, consume hooks and services via props/hooks
constants/  → fileTypes.ts, uploadStatus.ts, apiTypes.ts
app/(app)/  → page-level components (ingest, data, query, datasets)
```

**Data flow:** Page → Component → Hook → Service → Backend. Never skip a layer.

## Code Style

- Named exports, not default exports (exception: page components).
- Colocate types with the module that owns them. Shared types go in `constants/apiTypes.ts`.
- Prefer `interface` over `type` for object shapes.
- Error handling: user-friendly toast via `ui/Toast.tsx`, full error to `console.error` in dev only (`import.meta.env.DEV`).
- Use TanStack Query for all server state. Use Zustand for client-only state.

## Backend Endpoints (do NOT modify or mock)

```
POST /ingest/pcap              — single file upload
POST /ingest/pcap/batch        — batch file upload
WS   /ws/status/{job_id}       — job status stream
GET  /datasets/types           — list dataset types
GET  /datasets/{type}/tables   — tables for a type
GET  /datasets/{type}/tables/{name}?page=&pageSize=&sortBy=&sortDir=&filters=
POST /query                    — execute SQL
```

## Status Enum

`UPLOADED → QUEUED → PROCESSING → PARSED | FAILED`

## When Unsure

- Check `@architecture.md` for the full API contract and type definitions.
- Check `constants/apiTypes.ts` for shared interfaces.
- If a component needs data, add a TanStack Query hook — don't fetch inline.
- If a new service endpoint is needed, add it to `services/` and update `apiTypes.ts`.
